From 4a892dc10c6ead44f8b92a07c4b5d2eff6496784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik <ritvik2014@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:01:17 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/40] render: liquid glass optics traced like Apple's
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the bounded smoothstep push and body magnification with the
physically traced edge used by the closest Liquid Glass recreations
(kube.io): a convex squircle bevel, y = (1-(1-x)^4)^1/4, 'refraction' px
thick over 'bevel' px; a ray straight down refracts by Snell's law (IOR 1.5)
and lands h*tan(θ1-θ2) inward. The middle stays undistorted; the rim
squeezes and, nearest the edge, mirrors what is just inside. Dispersion is a
per-channel IOR spread. The rim samples the unblurred backdrop (second
texture unit) easing into the frosted middle, so lensing stays crisp over
frost. Light: broad top-left glint and opposite inner reflection on the
curved band, a silhouette hairline, and 1.18x vibrancy.
---
 src/render_helpers/framebuffer_effect.rs     |  35 ++++-
 src/render_helpers/shaders/liquid_glass.frag | 139 ++++++++++++-------
 src/render_helpers/shaders/mod.rs            |   1 +
 3 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

